SDL2: use the legacy GBM cursor/write allocation contract

SPDX-License-Identifier: Zlib
Local alteration for the pinned GBM 10.4 provider, whose header declares
CURSOR and WRITE but no LINEAR flag. Its gbm.h documents that gbm_bo_write
is guaranteed for CURSOR buffers. Do not invent a flag the provider does
not expose. Actual cursor allocation/scanout still requires native testing;
compilation and the headless contract probe cannot approve it.

--- a/src/video/kmsdrm/SDL_kmsdrmmouse.c
+++ b/src/video/kmsdrm/SDL_kmsdrmmouse.c
@@ -107,7 +107,9 @@
 
     dispdata->cursor_bo = KMSDRM_gbm_bo_create(viddata->gbm_dev,
                                                dispdata->cursor_w, dispdata->cursor_h,
-                                               GBM_FORMAT_ARGB8888, GBM_BO_USE_CURSOR | GBM_BO_USE_WRITE | GBM_BO_USE_LINEAR);
+                                               /* Local legacy-provider path: CURSOR
+                                                * guarantees gbm_bo_write support. */
+                                               GBM_FORMAT_ARGB8888, GBM_BO_USE_CURSOR | GBM_BO_USE_WRITE);
 
     if (!dispdata->cursor_bo) {
         SDL_SetError("Could not create GBM cursor BO");
